/*
 * DAOLib's namespaces, one line each, for the site's namespace list (DAOLib #45).
 * The headers' own comments describe files, not namespaces, so the namespaces'
 * descriptions live here. Doxygen reads this file; nothing compiles it.
 */

/// @namespace dao
/// Everything in DAOLib: the game's classes and the library's parts, each in a namespace of its own.

/// @namespace dao::abilities
/// Abilities: their names, whether a creature can use one now and what it costs, and cooldowns.

/// @namespace dao::animation
/// How long animations, attacks and abilities take a creature to play.

/// @namespace dao::attack
/// Melee and ranged attacks: reach, the approach to a target, turning to face it.

/// @namespace dao::camera
/// Smooth camera moves: panning to a creature, turning behind it, easing the zoom.

/// @namespace dao::clock
/// Pause or speed up the game's clock for effects, regeneration and their timers.

/// @namespace dao::commands
/// A creature's commands: when they start and end, the steps they run, and holding a spell's
/// conjure.

/// @namespace dao::data
/// The game's data tree, the named values its interface reads and writes.

/// @namespace dao::dialogue
/// Conversations, cutscenes and movies: watch them, steer which replies appear, skip them.

/// @namespace dao::effects
/// Temporary effects: list them on a creature, stop them wearing off, age them at once.

/// @namespace dao::equipment
/// Hear when equipment goes on or comes off a creature.

/// @namespace dao::events
/// The scripts' events (damage, perception, death and the rest), as callbacks.

/// @namespace dao::gda
/// The game's data tables (2DA/GDA): read a value by table, row and column.

/// @namespace dao::gui
/// The Flash interface: answer movies' calls into the game, call into movies, add screens.

/// @namespace dao::input
/// Key bindings of a plugin's own, and pointing the game's cursor pick at a pixel.

/// @namespace dao::journal
/// The journal's quests, current and completed.

/// @namespace dao::messages
/// The engine's messages: watch, intercept or send them.

/// @namespace dao::Module
/// The running game executable, and turning the library's address IDs into addresses in it.

/// @namespace dao::options
/// A plugin's own settings in the game's options screen.

/// @namespace dao::orders
/// Give orders as the player's clicks do: attack, use, cast, move.

/// @namespace dao::party
/// The party: who is selected and who the player controls.

/// @namespace dao::portraits
/// Frame a creature's portrait with a camera of your own.

/// @namespace dao::resources
/// Read a file as the game finds it, a mod's version over the game's.

/// @namespace dao::saves
/// A plugin's own data kept with the game's saves; listing saves, and saving or loading.

/// @namespace dao::script
/// Script commands from C++: call them, intercept them, replace them or add new ones.

/// @namespace dao::strings
/// A plugin's own text in the player's language, from talk tables beside its DLL.

/// @namespace dao::timers
/// The scripts' delayed events: hold them, deliver them on a clock of your own, trace them.

/// @namespace dao::tlk
/// The game's own text by string reference, in the player's language.

/// @namespace dao::vfx
/// Draw in the world with the game's visual effects: rings, reticles, any effect by row.

/// @namespace dao::world
/// The world's geometry: rays, line of sight, screen positions, paths and rooms.

/// @namespace dao::world::groups
/// The collision groups a ray can be tested against.
